 and builders. MasterBrand, Inc. was founded in 1954 and is headquartered in Beachwood, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. R. David Banyard Jr. | CEO, President & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 12K people. Revenue per employee of $216K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $9K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["MasterBrand, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.3B market cap on $2.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are contracting by -3.4pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The business throws off $118M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 7.33\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.4%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -3.4pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Price sits 862% above estimated fair value \u2014 n